P-6 (spec 017, the night shift; plan.md §10; research.md R-06; tasks.md T063): infra/account/iam.tf gains
h4-agent-plan, the plan-only role a night-shift plan runs as.

What it adds (FR-032):
  - local.plan_permission_set = "<ADMIN_PERMISSION_SET>", in iam.tf's locals beside laptop_permission_set. The
    repository doesn't hold your administrator permission set's name (spec 001's plan.md notes the same, for the
    state bucket's administrator-only clause), so
    write it there before you apply: IAM Identity Center, Permission sets, the one your h4reet-admin profile signs in
    with. Until you do, the role's precondition refuses the account root's plan, naming the local. A wrong name admits
    no one; it can't lock you out of anything.
  - its trust: only that set's role, AWSReservedSSO_<set>_<16 characters> under Identity Center's path (and with a
    Region's segment), by the pattern h4-laptop-bedrock's trust uses; sts:AssumeRole; max_session_duration 3600.
  - its permissions: AWS's ReadOnlyAccess, attached alone; an explicit deny of ssm:GetParameter, GetParameters,
    GetParametersByPath, GetParameterHistory, secretsmanager:GetSecretValue, and BatchGetSecretValue on "*" (IAM has no
    condition key for a parameter read's decryption, so the deny takes every value read; Terraform here reads none,
    rule T9); and s3:PutObject and s3:DeleteObject on arn:aws:s3:::h4reet-ai-tfstate-*/*.tflock only. The bucket's
    suffix is yours and isn't in the account root, so the grant names the bootstrap's bucket prefix.
  - its tags: component agent-plan, with project and environment from the provider's default_tags.
  - the file's header comment names it.
Your apply, then: a profile for the runner (PLAN_AWS_PROFILE) whose role_arn is h4-agent-plan and whose source is your
SSO session; the runbook (T061) has it.

Spec IDs: decision 1, FR-032, his Q4 answer taken as recommended (the plan takes the state's lock, *.tflock only),
the Assumptions' named deviation of Principle IV (an agent's command gets cloud access through a role assumed from his
SSO identity; ADR 0051).

Needed for: plan on. Not for the merge.

How to apply, on your own branch, from the repository's root (one line each):
  B=feat/017-g5-patches
  F=docs/merge-requests/2026-11-12-feat-017-p6.patch
  git show "refs/heads/$B:$F" > /tmp/p6.patch
  sha256sum /tmp/p6.patch
  patch -p1 --dry-run < /tmp/p6.patch
  patch -p1 < /tmp/p6.patch
Then write the set's name in infra/account/iam.tf, plan the account root as you do today, and apply.

